me","lead":"A national scheme change could force the council to abandon this implementation, wasting project costs and creating timing uncertainty around a major revenue collection system","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"11.4% of claimants will receive reduced support; collection risk if affordability worsens","lead":"Reduced support makes council tax less affordable for vulnerable residents; affordability problems typically increase arrears and reduce collection rates, affecting revenue stability","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The redesigned scheme is modeled as cost-neutral but costs are explicitly expected to fluctuate with residents' incomes","lead":"The council's net revenue available for services depends on stable Council Tax Support costs; if economic pressures worsen residents' incomes, costs could increase unpredictably, creating budget pressure","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Policy Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","headline":"Government is considering a national Council Tax Support scheme redesign that could supersede this local scheme","detail":"While no immediate national changes are planned, government has indicated that Council Tax Support schemes may be reviewed soon with the possibility of reintroducing a national scheme. This would render the current redesign project obsolete and force the council to adopt new rules.","category":"governance","matters":"A national scheme change could force the council to abandon this implementation, wasting project costs and creating timing uncertainty around a major revenue collection system","figures":"None","quote":"Whilst there are no immediate changes planned nationally for Council or Council tax Support Schemes, it has been suggested that these may be reviewed by government soon, with the possibility of a national scheme being re-introduced for Council Tax Support","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Policy Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","headline":"11.4% of claimants will receive reduced support; collection risk if affordability worsens","detail":"472 claimants (11.4% of 4,174) will receive reduced awards under the new scheme. The council will contact them and offer support including Crisis and Resilience Fund access and debt advice. However, residents unable to absorb a reduction in support create collection risk if they become unable to pay council tax.","category":"income","matters":"Reduced support makes council tax less affordable for vulnerable residents; affordability problems typically increase arrears and reduce collection rates, affecting revenue stability","figures":"472 claimants (11.4%) losing support; 3,225 claimants (77.2%) unchanged; 477 claimants (11.4%) gaining","quote":"All residents identified as losing out through these proposals will be contacted and invited to contribute to the consultation and invited to seek additional support to ensure they are maximising their income and offered debt advice.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Policy Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","headline":"The redesigned scheme is modeled as cost-neutral but costs are explicitly expected to fluctuate with residents' incomes","detail":"The proposed scheme costs \u00a34,712,334.39 versus current \u00a34,703,840.03 \u2014 a difference of -\u00a38,494.36. However, the council explicitly states that actual costs will move with local and national factors affecting residents' income, and notes it will need to monitor and potentially review the scheme in subsequent years.","category":"income","matters":"The council's net revenue available for services depends on stable Council Tax Support costs; if economic pressures worsen residents' incomes, costs could increase unpredictably, creating budget pressure","figures":"Proposed scheme cost \u00a34,712,334.39; current scheme \u00a34,703,840.03; modeled difference -\u00a38,494.36","quote":"This proposal has been modelled as a cost neutral scheme, although by its nature costs can fluctuate during the year depending on local and national factors impacting residents' income.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Policy Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","headline":"The current scheme creates administrative and collection complexity that makes it unfit for purpose","detail":"Reading's current scheme, unchanged since 2022/23, requires constant recalculations and new bills due to Universal Credit's fluctuating income. This complicates debt recovery and collection. The new banded scheme aims to reduce billing churn and improve collection rates through administrative simplification.","category":"income","matters":"Collection efficiency directly affects council cash flow and the predictability of revenue; complex billing and debt recovery processes increase arrears and reduce collection rates","figures":"Last year the council issued 8,500 council tax support adjustment notices against a caseload of just over 4,000 working age claimants","quote":"The current Council Tax Support Scheme is no longer fit for purpose, requiring regular changes to awards and the constant despatch of new bills, making it difficult for customers to understand or plan their finances as well as making administration and debt recovery complicated and expensive.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Policy Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Summary of the General Fund Budget and Forecast","paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41051/41051.pdf","headline":"Environmental & Commercial Services forecast to overspend by \u00a3950k","detail":"Forecast spend of \u00a319,574k against a budget of \u00a318,624k represents the second-largest operational directorate overspend in the council. The driver is not explained in this summary.","category":"overspend","matters":"A significant overspend in a commercial services area signals either cost inflation or commercial revenue underperformance, both material to financial planning and resilience.","figures":"Environmental & Commercial Services variance \u00a3950k","quote":"Environmental & Commercial Services 18,668 (44) 18,624 19,574 950","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Reading UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Government is considering a national Council Tax Support scheme redesign that could supersede this local scheme","lead":"A national scheme change could force the council to abandon this implementation, wasting project costs and creating timing uncertainty around a major revenue collection system","also":["19 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Governance Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":20,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Council Tax Support Scheme","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.reading.gov.uk/documents/s41059/41059.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":116,"news_drafts_total":3}}